{"availability":"available","full":"shipap/saas-starter-kit","name":"saas-starter-kit","description":"Multi-tenant SaaS starter with RBAC, teams, mock billing, API keys, audit logs, and isolated demos.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-01T14:10:53Z","updated":"2026-10-01T14:30:59Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://saas.rkn.fail","topics":["better-auth","docker","drizzle-orm","multi-tenant","nextjs","postgresql","rbac","saas","starter-kit","typescript"],"demo":"https://saas.rkn.fail/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:12.733Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:12.733Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:12.733Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:42:12.733Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Build a multi-tenant SaaS product without starting again with accounts, workspaces, team permissions, billing state and API access.","The starter demonstrates those foundations through Relay, a fictional B2B workspace console. Open the demo without a password, create projects, invite a teammate through a development outbox, switch roles, try mock plans and issue a real workspace API key. Every demo visitor gets an isolated sandbox. The next step for a client is adding their business-specific feature to this foundation.","Relay and its seeded people, organizations and activity are fictional. Billing is simulated and email stays in a development outbox; no real payments or messages are sent."],"features":["Better Auth email/password sessions and optional configured OAuth providers, separate from demo sessions.","Organization creation, switching and settings with membership checks on the server.","Centralized four-role authorization and protected ownership operations.","Projects with search, status filtering, create/edit/archive and permission-aware controls.","Expiring, one-use team invitations, role mana